WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.380
NHTSA is reviewing claims at Tesla Robotaxi Speed and School Zones, adding regulatory pressure on the service. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 633. Claims Journal says the agency is evaluating a petition that includes video of several incidents. The clips involve Tesla Cybercab and model y vehicles using automated systems. The preliminary probe covers an estimated 1000 vehicles from the 2026 model year.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.200
NHTSA has not yet decided whether to grant or deny the request for a full investigation.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.920
Tesla did not immediately respond to a request for comment.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:42.400
The agency has a separate investigation underway into the process and technical data Tesla

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.960
relied on when it self-certified the cybercab.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:52.200
Tesla Oracle reports that as of October 12, Tesla has registered 319 cybercabs in Texas.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:59.480
Texas. By the end of September, only 126 CyberCab units were operating in Austin. 420 Model

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:05.300
Y Robotaxies were active at that same point. The Texas total of autonomous cars operating

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:13.220
via the Tesla Robotaxi app now stands at 739. Tesla has paused the number of Model Y Robotaxies

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:19.600
at 420. The company stated floodgates are opening after sightings of multiple CyberCabs on an

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:25.040
Austin Street. Austin remains the only U.S. city where Tesla currently uses the CyberCab

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:29.960
for autonomous ride hailing. In a clip shared by Tesla Roddy, a passenger says,

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.960
hey, GROC, and ask the system to add laundry detergent to an Amazon cart. GROC confirms the

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:40.920
task is finished before the ride ends. The demo shows that integration working at night while

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:47.080
the vehicle drives itself. Not a Tesla app reports that Tesla's CyberCab Chief Engineer confirmed new

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:52.260
seats are in development. Additional very cool upgrades are also planned for the purpose-built

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:58.820
Robotaxi. Those updates were discussed during an X session. Tesla has paused new Model 3 premium

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:04.920
orders in Canada after exhausting its import quota, according to a thread on the Tesla Motors subreddit.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:12.780
Ordering is expected to resume in March 2027. The pause occurs despite more than 33,000 spots remaining

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:18.780
in the quota allocation. Yahoo News UK describes a new homeowner who bought a house with an installed

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:25.060
Tesla Powerwall and was nominated as the owner. The Powerwall, Gateway, and Charger would not appear

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:31.020
in the Tesla app. Replies on the Reddit thread pointed to a lost internet connection. Those replies

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:36.460
recommended using the setup app to reconnect the system. One user noted that the front cover must

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:42.660
be removed carefully to access the Wi-Fi password for a Powerwall 3. Another suggested separating

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:48.280
the 2.4 gigahertz and 5 gigahertz bands on the home router, because many modern routers

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:53.980
combine the bands by default. Taiwan Power Company placed an order for 260 Tesla

00:02:53.980 --> 00:03:00.020
Megapax, Tesla North Reports. The utility-scale battery systems will support grid stability

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:05.400
and renewable integration on the island. Tesla released plans for what would be Australia's

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:11.560
largest EV charging hub in Albary, Thirguna, according to ABC News. The site is intended

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.700
it to support growing electric vehicle traffic on major routes.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:20.700
Drive Tesla Canada reports Tesla's retail sales in China fell 9% in September compared

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.680
with the prior year.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:26.220
Exports from the Shanghai Factory rose 58% in the same period.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:32.160
Tesla's automations feature is ready for international release, but remains hidden behind a software

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:32.560
flag.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:38.340
Drive Tesla Canada says, the app lists multiple triggers and actions that users will be able

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.220
to combine once the flag is enabled.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:45.280
AutoBlog reports Tesla introduced new lease offers for the Model Y this month.

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:49.040
The offers apply to current inventory and new production vehicles.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:54.760
Tesla has begun installing centralized payment kiosks at supercharger locations in Canada,

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.900
according to Drive Tesla Canada.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:01.620
The kiosks allow drivers to pay without using the vehicle screen or the app.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:09.220
Torque News reports a cyber truck owner hauled his son's drumline gear and towed a trailer estimated at 5,500 pounds.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:15.900
the trip covered 103 miles in total. The truck consumed 81 kilowatt hours and arrived at the

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:23.560
charger with roughly 15% battery remaining. He started the day by charging from 73% to 89% and

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:29.600
bought 120 chicken nuggets for the students. Another cyber truck driver told Torque News he completed a

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:36.300
Maryland to Delray Beach trip while keeping the trailer attached at every stop. He towed 1,100 miles

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:42.600
without unhitching. The 14 charging sessions averaged 35 minutes each. The longest stop lasted

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:47.620
80 minutes. Tesla's navigation optimized the route for trailer-friendly superchargers

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:53.140
that allow pull-through charging. The objection writing itself is that Tesla is adding cybercabs

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:58.840
in Austin, while federal safety staff are still weighing a school-zone petition. A full investigation

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:04.420
has not been opened, and the request could still be denied. Stacked on top of that is a second

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:10.500
Federal look at how the CyberCab was self-certified. That combination is the regulatory risk, even

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:16.580
before any finding lands. Import quotas function as hard-volume caps that reset on fixed schedules,

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:21.760
rather than as flexible-demand signals. When a manufacturer exhausts its annual

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:26.840
allotment for a given model, new orders must wait for the next cycle even if customer interest

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:32.880
remains strong. The system creates an artificial inventory cliff. Production continues at the factory,

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:37.220
industry, yet vehicles cannot be registered for those buyers until the calendar advances.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:42.440
Dealers and customers experience that as a sudden stop rather than a gradual slowdown,

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:46.580
and the company loses the ability to match supply with immediate demand.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:52.060
Manufacturers that concentrate volume in one configuration risk hitting the ceiling earlier,

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:57.480
and a halt rather than a shift of allocations from other trims, shows the quota acting as

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:00.840
a binding production scheduler rather than a simple tariff.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:06.660
Before we go, the next decision on that school's own petition is whether NHTSA grants a full

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:08.460
investigation or turns it down.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:11.140
That covers it for today's Tesla developments.

